{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-45c26dc1-eb9a-4984-b5d8-56e92d26dd73","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b28e2cbc2ff5999d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-bgxd3ey4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004.md","content":"# Operator-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n\n## Description\n\nImplement self-provisioning of the default PostgreSQL/pgvector instance in the\nRHOAI-controlled operator layer for Gen AI Studio — the operator delivered by the\ndashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) — following the pattern the\nmodel-registry-operator uses for its auto-provisioned PostgreSQL. This epic exists only\nif the go/no-go decision selects the operator path (the modularization lands in time for\nthe target release). The database runs as a separate process from the OGX instance and\nis scoped per playground namespace.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Reconciler logic in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator that creates a\n  PostgreSQL Deployment (pgvector-capable), Service, credentials Secret, and persistent\n  storage in the playground's namespace when a playground with RAG is configured, using\n  the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that already includes pgvector\n  (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`) — no custom image build and no new pipeline\n  onboarding.\n- Lifecycle management via the reconciliation loop: the instance is created with the\n  playground and removed when the playground is deleted; secret/credential handling\n  follows the model-registry-operator pattern.\n- Per-namespace isolation: the database is reachable only within its own namespace; no\n  cross-namespace access.\n- Resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL\n  reference sizing, adjusted per the sprint-1 benchmark recommendation.\n- Disconnected-install support through the existing RELATED_IMAGE PostgreSQL image\n  reference mechanism already present in the operator CSV.\n- Expose the connection reference (credentials secret) for consumption by the playground\n  OGX instance's pgvector vector_io provider configuration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- With a playground with RAG configured, the operator provisions a running PostgreSQL\n  instance with the pgvector extension available in the playground's namespace —\n  including credentials secret and persistent storage — without any user action.\n- Deleting the playground removes its database instance and associated resources.\n- The database is reachable only from within its own namespace (isolation verified from\n  a second namespace).\n- Resource requests/limits on the provisioned instance match the benchmark-informed\n  recommendation derived from the model-registry-operator reference sizing.\n- The PostgreSQL image reference is overridable for disconnected installs via the\n  RELATED_IMAGE mechanism, verified by pointing it at an internal registry mirror.\n- No custom container image is built or onboarded as part of this epic (the existing\n  Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector is reused).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Strategy acceptance criterion: a default vector store is available out-of-the-box\n  without users manually provisioning or configuring external infrastructure.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store runs as a separate process,\n  decoupled from the OGX instance.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store is scoped appropriately for\n  multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation).\n- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store is lightweight enough for\n  resource-constrained environments.\n- Staff Engineer Input: self-provisioning follows the model-registry-operator pattern in\n  the RHOAI-controlled operator; the Red Hat PostgreSQL image already includes pgvector;\n  no Konflux onboarding needed; resource sizing references the model-registry-operator.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- This epic exists only on the operator-path outcome of the go/no-go decision; the\n  delivery timing of the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) is outside\n  this strategy's control and gates whether this work can begin.\n- The operator layer this epic extends is delivered by RHAISTRAT-7164; coordinate the\n  provisioning reconciler design with that strategy's owners to avoid conflicting\n  controller designs.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64289,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-899742fad80db074","agent_id":"aecdf30ec811431c0","session_id":"dea9077a-5606-465d-8634-40ab1d74f5b7","uuid":"68bf358e-b086-425c-b666-1f287a0d4541","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:19:30.097Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
