{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8f356291-9fbe-445e-ace0-d1ab9aed8980","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d7c0ca429cd44d0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-bgxd3ey4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E005.md","content":"# End-to-end validation of Playground RAG with the operator-provisioned default vector store\n\n## Description\n\nValidate the complete out-of-the-box experience on the operator path: Gen AI Studio\nplayground RAG workflows function against the operator-managed default pgvector-backed\nvector store with no loss of current capability and no manual setup steps, in\nmulti-tenant and resource-constrained conditions. This epic exists only on the\noperator-path outcome of the go/no-go decision.\n\n## Scope\n\n- End-to-end test scenarios for playground RAG against the default store: document\n  upload, embedding, indexing, retrieval, and grounded generation.\n- Regression comparison against the current capability set: every playground RAG\n  capability available with the inline provider passes with the default store.\n- Multi-tenant verification: two playgrounds in different namespaces cannot access each\n  other's vector data (per-namespace isolation).\n- Resource-constrained environment verification: the playground and its default store\n  operate within the benchmark-informed resource envelope on a constrained cluster.\n- Disconnected-install validation of the full default-store path (image reference\n  override plus playground RAG workflow).\n- Performance sanity check against the captured inline Milvus baseline: ingestion and\n  retrieval within the same order of magnitude (development-experimentation scope; no\n  latency SLAs).\n- A published validation report summarizing results and any remediation taken.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A freshly configured playground with RAG works end to end with zero manual database\n  setup or configuration steps.\n- The full existing playground RAG capability set passes the end-to-end suite against\n  the default store with no functional regression.\n- Per-namespace isolation is verified: cross-namespace access to another playground's\n  vector data fails.\n- The playground and its default store operate within the recommended resource envelope\n  on a resource-constrained cluster.\n- The disconnected-install scenario passes with the PostgreSQL image reference pointed\n  at an internal registry mirror.\n- Measured ingestion and retrieval performance is within the same order of magnitude as\n  the captured inline Milvus baseline.\n- The validation report is published and states pass/fail for each criterion above.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Strategy acceptance criterion: Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with\n  the default vector store with no loss of current capability.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion: a default vector store is available out-of-the-box\n  without manual provisioning or configuration.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store is scoped appropriately for\n  multi-tenant environments.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store is lightweight enough for\n  resource-constrained environments.\n- Strategy success criterion: users experience no functional regression when inline\n  providers are removed from the OGX distribution.\n- Staff Engineer Input: validate pgvector only for Gen AI Studio Playground RAG\n  workflows (Auto Rag compatibility is out of scope, deferred to RHAISTRAT-7824);\n  benchmark criterion is order-of-magnitude, not a threshold.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Requires the pgvector provider wiring, the operator-managed provisioning, and the\n  inline Milvus baseline to be in place before the comparison scenarios can run.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65290,"output_tokens":0},"con