{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b803c10aacc9b84","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Configure the pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground OGX\n4\t  instances\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Configure the pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tWire the pgvector remote vector store provider into the OGX instances the gen-ai BFF\n35\tcreates for playgrounds with RAG, so vector storage is served by a separate\n36\tPostgreSQL-backed process instead of the inline provider bundled in the OGX distribution\n37\timage. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the existing remote vector store implementation is\n38\tlargely reusable and the majority of the overall effort is database provisioning (handled\n39\tseparately, per the selected provisioning approach); this epic covers the provider\n40\tconfiguration wiring only.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- In the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance creation for playgrounds (the playground\n45\t  configuration path in the dashboard's gen-ai BFF), activate the pgvector vector_io\n46\t  provider (the remote `remote::pgvector` provider via its `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` environment\n47\t  guard) when RAG is configured for the playground.\n48\t- Point the provider at a PostgreSQL connection reference (credentials secret) supplied\n49\t  by whichever provisioning mechanism is selected — operator-provisioned, BFF-provisioned,\n50\t  or user-provided — so the wiring itself is approach-independent.\n51\t- Leave the OGX application storage configuration untouched (existing SQLite defaults\n52\t  for key-value and SQL storage). No vector/application storage consolidation and no\n53\t  SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration: vector storage and application storage are independent\n54\t  configurations.\n55\t- Verify the OGX distribution's remote pgvector provider requires no distribution-side\n56\t  code change (the provider ships in the distribution); raise any gaps found with the\n57\t  OGX maintainers.\n58\t- Unit and integration tests for the provider configuration path, including the negative\n59\t  case (RAG disabled → provider not activated, no database reference required).\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- When the gen-ai BFF creates an OGXServer instance for a playground with RAG enabled,\n64\t  the created instance activates the pgvector vector_io provider backed by the referenced\n65\t  PostgreSQL connection, and vector storage is served by that separate database rather\n66\t  than an inline provider.\n67\t- When RAG is not enabled for a playground, the pgvector provider is not activated and\n68\t  no database reference is required.\n69\t- Application storage settings of created OGXServer instances remain on their existing\n70\t  defaults; no storage migration or consolidation is introduced.\n71\t- The connection reference is consumed generically: operator-provisioned,\n72\t  BFF-provisioned, and user-provided PostgreSQL instances all work without changes to\n73\t  this wiring.\n74\t- The provider configuration is reversible by configuration alone (switching to another\n75\t  remote vector provider requires no code change), preserving a rollback path while\n76\t  inline providers are being removed from the distribution.\n77\t- Tests covering the activated, deactivated, and connection-reference-consumption cases\n78\t  pass in the dashboard CI.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store runs as a separate process,\n83\t  decoupled from the OGX instance (not an inline provider).\n84\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with\n85\t  the default vector store (this epic delivers the provider integration those workflows\n86\t  run against).\n87\t- Staff Engineer Input: vector_io provider configuration is independent of the OGX\n88\t  application storage backend; the existing remote vector store implementation is\n89\t  reusable; the effort focus is provisioning, not provider integration.\n90\t\n91\t## Risks / Notes\n92\t\n93\t- If verification finds the distribution's pgvector provider incomplete for the\n94\t  playground's usage, a distribution-side change may be needed after all — escalate\n95\t  immediately, as it would add an OGX work stream not currently in this decomposition.\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f4737d4ae1466a3","agent_id":"af7df5a568cec00a3","session_id":"dea9077a-5606-465d-8634-40ab1d74f5b7","uuid":"9f8e5577-9dc9-405a-9022-2525149a5e30","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:10:38.583Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b803c10aacc9b84","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
