{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a30f051227610366","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Capture inline Milvus baseline and benchmark pgvector for Playground RAG workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Capture inline Milvus baseline and benchmark pgvector for Playground RAG workloads\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tBefore inline providers are removed from the OGX distribution (RHAISTRAT-7474), capture\n30\tthe performance baseline of the inline Milvus vector store on representative Playground\n31\tRAG workloads, then benchmark a pgvector-backed remote vector store on the same\n32\tworkloads and verify it is in the same order of magnitude. The outcome is a benchmark\n33\treport and a concrete resource-sizing recommendation for the default PostgreSQL/pgvector\n34\tinstance. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the default store targets development\n35\texperimentation: no strict latency SLAs (p50/p95/p99) apply, and typical Playground RAG\n36\tusage involves small document sets where a flat scan (no index) is sufficient.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Define representative Playground RAG benchmark workloads reflecting typical usage:\n41\t  small document sets, ingestion (embedding + indexing) and retrieval (query) phases,\n42\t  flat scan without a vector index.\n43\t- Capture the inline Milvus provider's performance baseline on those workloads. This is\n44\t  time-sensitive: it must be completed before the inline provider removal lands in the\n45\t  OGX distribution.\n46\t- Provision a development pgvector instance (may be manually stood up for the benchmark;\n47\t  no dependency on the production provisioning approach) and run the same workloads\n48\t  against it through the remote vector_io provider path.\n49\t- Compare ingestion and retrieval measurements between the inline Milvus baseline and\n50\t  pgvector; the pass criterion is same order of magnitude, not a specific threshold.\n51\t- Produce a PostgreSQL resource requests/limits recommendation for the default instance,\n52\t  starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource sizing and adjusted\n53\t  per the benchmark results.\n54\t- Document methodology so both measurements are reproducible.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A benchmark report exists documenting the workloads, methodology, the inline Milvus\n59\t  baseline measurements, and the pgvector measurements.\n60\t- The report explicitly states pass/fail against the same-order-of-magnitude criterion\n61\t  for both ingestion and retrieval.\n62\t- The report includes a concrete resource requests/limits recommendation for the default\n63\t  PostgreSQL/pgvector instance, derived from the model-registry-operator reference sizing\n64\t  and the measured results.\n65\t- The inline Milvus baseline is captured before inline providers are removed from the\n66\t  OGX distribution, and the methodology section is sufficient to reproduce both\n67\t  measurements.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store is lightweight enough to run\n72\t  in resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead (the\n73\t  sizing recommendation is the deliverable that informs it).\n74\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: no loss of current capability (verified at the\n75\t  order-of-magnitude level against the inline provider baseline).\n76\t- Staff Engineer Input: sprint-1 benchmark scope — capture the inline Milvus baseline\n77\t  and verify pgvector is in the same order of magnitude; latency-threshold, corpus-size,\n78\t  and index-type open questions removed; resource sizing references the\n79\t  model-registry-operator.\n80\t\n81\t## Risks / Notes\n82\t\n83\t- Time-boxed window: if the inline provider removal lands before the baseline is\n84\t  captured, the comparison loses its reference point and an older distribution image\n85\t  must be used to reconstruct it.\n86\t- If pgvector is not in the same order of magnitude, the default-store approach needs\n87\t  remediation (sizing adjustment, or escalation to reconsider the default) — this is a\n88\t  fix-and-retry outcome recorded in the report, not a re-planning trigger by itself.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f4737d4ae1466a3","agent_id":"af7df5a568cec00a3","session_id":"dea9077a-5606-465d-8634-40ab1d74f5b7","uuid":"827013fd-72f0-45c4-b7d4-930340d33630","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:10:42.582Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a30f051227610366","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
