{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be408a3a3a19e874","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E005\n3\ttitle: End-to-end validation of Playground RAG with the BFF-provisioned default vector\n4\t  store\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: B\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004\n16\tgate_failure_impact:\n17\t  action: remove\n18\t  fallback_approach: If the BFF-managed path is not selected, this validation epic\n19\t    is replaced by the equivalent validation against whichever provisioning approach\n20\t    the go/no-go decision selects.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: 1\n27\t  external_dependency: 0\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 6\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\t---\n37\t# End-to-end validation of Playground RAG with the BFF-provisioned default vector store\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tValidate the complete out-of-the-box experience on the BFF-managed path: Gen AI Studio\n42\tplayground RAG workflows function against the BFF-provisioned default pgvector-backed\n43\tvector store with no loss of current capability and no manual setup steps, in\n44\tmulti-tenant and resource-constrained conditions, including the BFF lifecycle behaviors\n45\t(cleanup on playground deletion, database pod restart). This epic exists only on the\n46\tBFF-managed outcome of the go/no-go decision.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- End-to-end test scenarios for playground RAG against the default store: document\n51\t  upload, embedding, indexing, retrieval, and grounded generation.\n52\t- Regression comparison against the current capability set: every playground RAG\n53\t  capability available with the inline provider passes with the default store.\n54\t- Multi-tenant verification: two playgrounds in different namespaces cannot access each\n55\t  other's vector data (per-namespace isolation).\n56\t- Lifecycle verification specific to BFF-managed provisioning: deleting a playground\n57\t  cleans up its database resources; a database pod restart does not break the playground\n58\t  or lose its stored vectors.\n59\t- Resource-constrained environment verification: the playground and its default store\n60\t  operate within the benchmark-informed resource envelope on a constrained cluster.\n61\t- Performance sanity check against the captured inline Milvus baseline: ingestion and\n62\t  retrieval within the same order of magnitude (development-experimentation scope; no\n63\t  latency SLAs).\n64\t- A published validation report summarizing results and any remediation taken.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- A freshly configured playground with RAG works end to end with zero manual database\n69\t  setup or configuration steps.\n70\t- The full existing playground RAG capability set passes the end-to-end suite against\n71\t  the default store with no functional regression.\n72\t- Per-namespace isolation is verified: cross-namespace access to another playground's\n73\t  vector data fails.\n74\t- Playground deletion removes the provisioned database resources, and a database pod\n75\t  restart recovers without data loss or manual intervention.\n76\t- The playground and its default store operate within the recommended resource envelope\n77\t  on a resource-constrained cluster.\n78\t- Measured ingestion and retrieval performance is within the same order of magnitude as\n79\t  the captured inline Milvus baseline.\n80\t- The validation report is published and states pass/fail for each criterion above.\n81\t\n82\t## HLR Traceability\n83\t\n84\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with\n85\t  the default vector store with no loss of current capability.\n86\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: a default vector store is available out-of-the-box\n87\t  without manual provisioning or configuration.\n88\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store is scoped appropriately for\n89\t  multi-tenant environments.\n90\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store is lightweight enough for\n91\t  resource-constrained environments.\n92\t- Strategy success criterion: users experience no functional regression when inline\n93\t  providers are removed from the OGX distribution.\n94\t- Staff Engineer Input: validate pgvector only for Gen AI Studio Playground RAG\n95\t  workflows (Auto Rag compatibility is out of scope, deferred to RHAISTRAT-7824);\n96\t  benchmark criterion is order-of-magnitude, not a threshold; BFF lifecycle behaviors\n97\t  (cleanup, restarts) need verification.\n98\t\n99\t## Risks / Notes\n100\t\n101\t- Requires the pgvector provider wiring, the BFF-managed provisioning, and the inline\n102\t  Milvus baseline to be in place before the comparison scenarios can run.\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f4737d4ae1466a3","agent_id":"af7df5a568cec00a3","session_id":"dea9077a-5606-465d-8634-40ab1d74f5b7","uuid":"327f26f6-8a9d-4564-87d4-01e3242b1e3f","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:54:02.789Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-be408a3a3a19e874","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
