{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6fbb86cb7eded80","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8004: Default Vector Store for Gen AI Studio\n10\t\n11\t## Staff Engineer Input Override Log\n12\t\n13\tThe Staff Engineer Input section is non-empty and takes precedence over the AI-generated\n14\tstrategy (whose full attachment was not available — see Health Warnings). Overrides applied:\n15\t\n16\t1. **Auto Rag decoupled.** Auto Rag removed from affected components, acceptance criteria,\n17\t   and validation requirements; Auto Rag/pgvector compatibility is deferred to\n18\t   RHAISTRAT-7824 (targeting the next release). Only Gen AI Studio Playground RAG\n19\t   workflows are validated in this strategy.\n20\t2. **PostgreSQL is new work, not an extension.** OGX defaults to SQLite for application\n21\t   storage; the claim that every OGX instance already requires PostgreSQL is incorrect.\n22\t   Introducing PostgreSQL/pgvector is new provisioning work.\n23\t3. **No custom image build, no Konflux onboarding.** The existing Red Hat PostgreSQL\n24\t   image (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`) includes pgvector; the\n25\t   model-registry-operator already auto-provisions it, and the RELATED_IMAGE reference\n26\t   exists for disconnected installs. The 1-2 sprint image-onboarding estimate is eliminated.\n27\t4. **Vector storage is independent of application storage.** Only the vector_io provider\n28\t   (`remote::pgvector` via `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`) is configured; application storage stays on\n29\t   SQLite. All SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration/consolidation concerns are removed.\n30\t5. **Performance thresholds removed.** The default store is for development\n31\t   experimentation; no latency SLAs. The sprint-1 benchmark verifies pgvector is in the\n32\t   same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline; flat scan (no index) suffices.\n33\t6. **Provisioning approach is conditional on RHAISTRAT-7164.** Operator-pattern\n34\t   self-provisioning requires the RHOAI-controlled operator from the dashboard operator\n35\t   modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164, In Progress) — a hard dependency. If it does not land\n36\t   in time, fallbacks are BFF-managed provisioning (guardrails pattern) or bring-your-own\n37\t   PostgreSQL. A go/no-go gate is to be defined in sprint planning.\n38\t7. **Resource sizing** starts from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL\n39\t   requests/limits, adjusted by the sprint-1 benchmark.\n40\t8. **Platform-provided shared PostgreSQL via DSC** is the long-term direction but will\n41\t   not be available until the following release; any provisioning built here must be\n42\t   portable to it (consume a connection string rather than assume self-provisioning).\n43\t\n44\t## Epic List\n45\t\n46\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n47\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n48\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E001 | Go/no-go decision: provisioning approach for the default vector store | Investigation | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n49\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 | Configure the pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances | Implementation | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Capture inline Milvus baseline and benchmark pgvector for Playground RAG workloads | Investigation | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n51\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E004 | Document the default vector store and the migration path to production vector databases | Implementation (docs-authoring) | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 | Operator-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds | Implementation (branch A) | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n53\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E005 | End-to-end validation of Playground RAG with the operator-provisioned default vector store | Implementation (branch A) | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n54\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds | Implementation (branch B) | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n55\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E005 | End-to-end validation of Playground RAG with the BFF-provisioned default vector store | Implementation (branch B) | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n56\t\n57\tMain plan: 4 epics (E001-E004). Conditional branches: 4 epics (2 per branch).\n58\t`epic_count` counts main-plan epics only (branch epics are not standalone Jira issues;\n59\tthey are attached to E001 as a plan document).\n60\t\n61\t## Dependency DAG\n62\t\n63\t```mermaid\n64\tgraph TD\n65\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: provisioning go/no-go\"]\n66\t    E002[\"E002 Implementation: pgvector provider wiring\"]\n67\t    E003[\"E003 Investigation: Milvus baseline + pgvector benchmark\"]\n68\t    E004[\"E004 docs: default store + migration path\"]\n69\t    BRA4[\"BRANCH-A-E004 operator provisioning\"]\n70\t    BRA5[\"BRANCH-A-E005 E2E validation (operator)\"]\n71\t    BRB4[\"BRANCH-B-E004 BFF-managed provisioning\"]\n72\t    BRB5[\"BRANCH-B-E005 E2E validation (BFF)\"]\n73\t\n74\t    E001 --> BRA4\n75\t    E001 --> BRA5\n76\t    E001 --> BRB4\n77\t    E001 --> BRB5\n78\t    E001 --> E004\n79\t    E002 --> BRA5\n80\t    E002 --> BRB5\n81\t    E002 --> E004\n82\t    BRA4 --> BRA5\n83\t    BRB4 --> BRB5\n84\t```\n85\t\n86\tE003 (benchmark) is deliberately a root with no outgoing edges: its outcome adjusts\n87\tresource sizing and confirms the order-of-magnitude performance assumption but does not\n88\tchange which epics exist or what they do — per the Step 3 decision rule it is expressed\n89\tas acceptance-criterion gates (\"resource requests/limits per the benchmark\n90\trecommendation\", \"performance within the same order of magnitude\") on the provisioning\n91\tand validation epics, not as DAG edges