{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8043605fbe448973","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Operator-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) does\n16\t    not land in time for the target release, drop this branch and use the BFF-managed\n17\t    provisioning path; bring-your-own PostgreSQL is the further fallback.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 0\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Operator-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplement self-provisioning of the default PostgreSQL/pgvector instance in the\n39\tRHOAI-controlled operator layer for Gen AI Studio — the operator delivered by the\n40\tdashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) — following the pattern the\n41\tmodel-registry-operator uses for its auto-provisioned PostgreSQL. This epic exists only\n42\tif the go/no-go decision selects the operator path (the modularization lands in time for\n43\tthe target release). The database runs as a separate process from the OGX instance and\n44\tis scoped per playground namespace.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Reconciler logic in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator that creates a\n49\t  PostgreSQL Deployment (pgvector-capable), Service, credentials Secret, and persistent\n50\t  storage in the playground's namespace when a playground with RAG is configured, using\n51\t  the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that already includes pgvector\n52\t  (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`) — no custom image build and no new pipeline\n53\t  onboarding.\n54\t- Lifecycle management via the reconciliation loop: the instance is created with the\n55\t  playground and removed when the playground is deleted; secret/credential handling\n56\t  follows the model-registry-operator pattern.\n57\t- Per-namespace isolation: the database is reachable only within its own namespace; no\n58\t  cross-namespace access.\n59\t- Resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL\n60\t  reference sizing, adjusted per the sprint-1 benchmark recommendation.\n61\t- Disconnected-install support through the existing RELATED_IMAGE PostgreSQL image\n62\t  reference mechanism already present in the operator CSV.\n63\t- Expose the connection reference (credentials secret) for consumption by the playground\n64\t  OGX instance's pgvector vector_io provider configuration.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- With a playground with RAG configured, the operator provisions a running PostgreSQL\n69\t  instance with the pgvector extension available in the playground's namespace —\n70\t  including credentials secret and persistent storage — without any user action.\n71\t- Deleting the playground removes its database instance and associated resources.\n72\t- The database is reachable only from within its own namespace (isolation verified from\n73\t  a second namespace).\n74\t- Resource requests/limits on the provisioned instance match the benchmark-informed\n75\t  recommendation derived from the model-registry-operator reference sizing.\n76\t- The PostgreSQL image reference is overridable for disconnected installs via the\n77\t  RELATED_IMAGE mechanism, verified by pointing it at an internal registry mirror.\n78\t- No custom container image is built or onboarded as part of this epic (the existing\n79\t  Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector is reused).\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: a default vector store is available out-of-the-box\n84\t  without users manually provisioning or configuring external infrastructure.\n85\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store runs as a separate process,\n86\t  decoupled from the OGX instance.\n87\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store is scoped appropriately for\n88\t  multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation).\n89\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: the default vector store is lightweight enough for\n90\t  resource-constrained environments.\n91\t- Staff Engineer Input: self-provisioning follows the model-registry-operator pattern in\n92\t  the RHOAI-controlled operator; the Red Hat PostgreSQL image already includes pgvector;\n93\t  no Konflux onboarding needed; resource sizing references the model-registry-operator.\n94\t\n95\t## Risks / Notes\n96\t\n97\t- This epic exists only on the operator-path outcome of the go/no-go decision; the\n98\t  delivery timing of the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) is outside\n99\t  this strategy's control and gates whether this work can begin.\n100\t- The operator layer this epic extends is delivered by RHAISTRAT-7164; coordinate the\n101\t  provisioning reconciler design with that strategy's owners to avoid conflicting\n102\t  controller designs.\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97085c80c2e4a002","agent_id":"aa401dc28139df828","session_id":"dea9077a-5606-465d-8634-40ab1d74f5b7","uuid":"41f76d22-d196-4e07-a0e1-aca874972444","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:07:25.805Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8043605fbe448973","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
