{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9b6f5281-d044-4ba0-b74c-8047b308ef8d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1ef1886a7423af0","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-bgxd3ey4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-decomposition.md","old_string":"    E001 --> BRA4\n    E001 --> BRA5\n    E001 --> BRB4\n    E001 --> BRB5\n    E001 --> E004\n    E002 --> BRA5\n    E002 --> BRB5\n    E002 --> E004\n    BRA4 --> BRA5\n    BRB4 --> BRB5\n```\n\nE003 (benchmark) is deliberately a root with no outgoing edges: its outcome adjusts\nresource sizing and confirms the order-of-magnitude performance assumption but does not\nchange which epics exist or what they do — per the Step 3 decision rule it is expressed\nas acceptance-criterion gates (\"resource requests/limits per the benchmark\nrecommendation\", \"performance within the same order of magnitude\") on the provisioning\nand validation epics, not as DAG edges.","new_string":"    E001 --> BRA4\n    E001 --> BRA5\n    E001 --> BRB4\n    E001 --> BRB5\n    E001 --> E004\n    E002 --> BRA5\n    E002 --> BRB5\n    E002 --> E004\n    E003 --> BRA4\n    E003 --> BRA5\n    E003 --> BRB4\n    E003 --> BRB5\n    E003 --> E004\n    BRA4 --> BRA5\n    BRB4 --> BRB5\n```\n\nE003 is an Implementation that produces concrete deliverables (the benchmark\nreport with the inline Milvus baseline measurements and the PostgreSQL\nresource-sizing recommendation). Its outcome does not change which epics exist\nor what they do — a failed comparison is a fix-and-retry outcome — so it gates\nnothing. But its deliverables are consumed as inputs by downstream epics: the\nprovisioning epics build their resource requests/limits from the sizing\nrecommendation, the validation epics verify against the captured baseline, and\nthe documentation draws on the benchmark conclusions. A benchmark report is not\na build-pipeline output consumed as content (the Rule 13 carve-out for\nattestations/digests does not apply), so these are real data dependencies\ncarried as DAG edges (Rule 13), not AC gates."}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56162,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97085c80c2e4a002","agent_id":"aa401dc28139df828","session_id":"dea9077a-5606-465d-8634-40ab1d74f5b7","uuid":"5a02017f-a4cb-41f6-b3da-313db0a13890","timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:28:10.500Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
